within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L04A_Immunosuppressants.L04AF01_Tofacitinib;
model Tofacitinib "Tofacitinib — default model: Tofacitinib_Xie2019_reference"
  extends Tofacitinib_Xie2019_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of tofacitinib: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L04A_Immunosuppressants.L04AF01_Tofacitinib.Tofacitinib_Xie2019_reference\">Tofacitinib_Xie2019_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of tofacitinib in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Tofacitinib_Chang2024_estimate</code></li><li><code>Tofacitinib_Chang2024_tofacitinib_5_mg_oral_solutionp</code></li><li><code>Tofacitinib_Chang2024_tofacitinib_5_mg_tablet</code></li><li><code>Tofacitinib_Xie2019_reference</code></li></ul><h4>About tofacitinib</h4><p>Tofacitinib is a JAK inhibitor immunosuppressant used to treat rheumatoid arthritis and ulcerative colitis, and has also been studied for conditions such as alopecia areata. It is an approved medicine, authorised in the European Union for rheumatoid arthritis, and carries a boxed warning.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3530324\">Wikidata Q3530324</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Tofacitinib\">Tofacitinib</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Tofacitinib;
